.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt GIT-WT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm git-wt
.Nd create or switch to a typed, provisioned git worktree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm git wt
.Op Fl -from Ar ref
.Op Fl -no-provision | Fl -provision-only
.Ar type
.Ar name
.Nm git wt
.Fl -remove
.Op Ar type Op Ar name
.Nm git wt
.Fl -init Ar zsh | bash
.Nm git wt
.Fl -version | Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks out branch
.Ar type Ns / Ns Ar name
in its own worktree and prints that worktree's absolute path on stdout.
All progress goes to stderr, so the output can be captured:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cd "$(git wt feat 1234-login)"
.Ed
.Pp
New worktrees live under the main checkout at
.Pa .worktrees/ Ns Ar type Ns / Ns Ar name ,
no matter which worktree
.Nm
is run from, so every worktree is a sibling and none is nested inside another.
If the branch is already checked out in any worktree, that worktree's path is
printed and nothing is created.
.Pp
The branch is resolved in order: an existing local branch, then a branch on
the remote (tracked locally), then a new branch from
.Ar ref
if
.Fl -from
was given, otherwise from the default branch named by
.Li origin/HEAD
(the local copy of that branch when one exists).
New branches get no upstream.
.Ss Setup of a new worktree
.Bl -bullet
.It
Adds
.Pa /.worktrees/
to
.Pa .git/info/exclude
if it is not already ignored.
.It
Copies gitignored files that a fresh checkout lacks, when they exist in the
main checkout:
.Pa config/master.key ,
.Pa config/credentials/{development,test}.key ,
.Pa .env ,
.Pa .env.local ,
.Pa .env.development.local ,
.Pa .env_overrides.rb ,
.Pa .vscode/settings.json .
.It
Clones
.Pa storage/
(local Active Storage blobs and Rails 8 SQLite databases) using APFS
copy-on-write, falling back to a plain copy.
.It
Runs the repository's
.Pa bin/worktree-setup ,
or
.Ql bin/setup --skip-server
if there is no such hook, or
.Ql bundle install
if there is only a
.Pa Gemfile .
The hook must be idempotent.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -from Ar ref
Start a new branch from
.Ar ref
(a branch, tag or commit; use
.Li HEAD
to branch from the current worktree).
Ignored with a warning if the branch already exists.
.It Fl -no-provision
Create the worktree and print its path, but skip the setup hook.
Exits 3 instead of 0 if the worktree already existed.
.It Fl -provision-only
Run the setup hook in the existing worktree for
.Ar type Ns / Ns Ar name .
.It Fl -remove Op Ar type Op Ar name
Remove the worktree for branch
.Ar type Ns / Ns Ar name ,
every worktree under
.Pa .worktrees/ Ns Ar type ,
or, with no arguments, every worktree under
.Pa .worktrees/ .
Each goes through
.Ql git worktree remove ,
which refuses one with modified or untracked files; the rest are still removed.
Each removed worktree's branch is then deleted with
.Ql git branch -d ,
which keeps a branch that is not merged.
Prints the main checkout's path, so
.Ic wt
leaves a removed worktree; exits 3 under
.Fl -no-provision .
.It Fl -init Ar zsh | bash
Print a
.Ic wt
shell function that runs
.Nm
and then changes into the worktree, setting it up after the
.Ic cd
so an interrupted setup still leaves you in place.
Add it to your shell startup file:
.Dl eval \&"$(git wt --init zsh)"
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl h
Print a usage line.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PORT
Set for the setup hook to a stable port derived from the branch name
(3001\(en3900), so dev servers in different worktrees do not collide.
The hook decides where to persist it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The worktree is ready, or already existed.
.It 1
Usage error, not inside a git repository, or
.Fl -remove
matched nothing or could not remove a worktree.
.It 3
With
.Fl -no-provision :
the worktree already existed, or
.Fl -remove
succeeded, so there is nothing to provision.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start work in a new sibling worktree from anywhere in the repository:
.Dl git wt feat 1234-login
.Pp
Spin off a follow-up branch from the one you are on:
.Dl git wt --from HEAD feat 1234-login-part-2
.Pp
Open a new session of some tool in a fresh worktree:
.Dl cd \&"$(git wt fix 99-typo)" && $EDITOR .
.Pp
Clean up after every feature branch at once:
.Dl git wt --remove feat
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git-worktree 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Worktrees share the Postgres databases named in
.Pa config/database.yml
unless the repository's setup hook gives each worktree its own.
.Pp
A SQLite database being written by a running server can be copied in an
inconsistent state.
